[tool_result]1	# Simulation Library CLI Full Reference (`python -m bda`) 2	 3	> Read on demand per the SKILL.md Section 4 guidance. The simulation library package lives in this skill's `scripts/bda/` (pip-editable-installed to this path; `python -m bda` invokes it). 4	 5	## General conventions 6	 7	- Invocation (Bash tool, repo root): `.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m bda <subcommand> ...`; all subcommands listed via `-m bda --help` 8	- The parameter bridge is a protocol rule (PyBaMM parameter-name mapping table in SKILL.md Section 1, Step 2); it has no CLI command. 9	- **Must use the Bash tool for simulation and render commands**: the PowerShell tool in this environment is guardrail-limited (`$()` subexpressions, `Set-Location`, `&` multi-operations are all blocked and unapprovable); if only PowerShell is available, the session tool allowlist is abnormal (resume rotation restores it) — retry with Bash first. 10	- JSON is the contract: all inputs/outputs are UTF-8 JSON files; `--out` specifies the output path; each step can be rerun independently. 11	- Same parameters must be reused (spec 5.2 invariant 3): all `run-*` commands check the store cache first, reusing on hit without recomputation. Cache directory = `cache/` under the `--out` file's directory (key = command parameter combination: run-pyamm: params+protocol+base+mode+thermal+plating; run-mlp: smiles+model; run-xtb: smiles; run-orca: smiles+charge+mult+functional; run-md: box+t_ns+engine; run-comp: candidates). Corrupt cache files (invalid JSON / non-object) are treated as misses and rewritten. 12	- Error convention: parameter/validation failures print `bda error: <reason>` to stderr with exit code 1; missing input files or missing JSON keys terminate with a Python traceback — read the last few output lines to locate the cause, fix per the hint, and rerun. 13	- Environment dependencies: `run-xtb` needs the xtb binary on PATH; `run-orca` needs orca on PATH; `run-md` needs gmx on PATH and a corresponding .itp template in the skill's `scripts/bda/simulators/data/opls/`. 14	 15	## Stage 2 funnel judgment (no CLI command) 16	 17	Funnel judgment (hard elimination lines + three-model heterogeneous voting) is executed per protocol rules — see SKILL.md Section 1, Step 1: run `run-mlp --model mace`, `run-mlp --model chgnet`, `run-xtb` for real, in order (same candidate list), then judge directly by reading the three output JSONs. No CLI command, no merged file needed. 18	 19	## run-pyamm — cell simulation 20	 21	``` 22	bda run-pyamm --params PARAMS --protocol PROTOCOL [--base BASE] [--mode MODE] [--thermal THERMAL] [--plating] [--cycles N] --out OUT 23	``` 24	 25	- `--base`: PyBaMM parameter-set name (default `Chen2020`); **the case configuration's `base_params` field must be passed verbatim to `--base`** (e.g., `--base ORegan2022`). Parameter names from the parameter bridge mapping table (SKILL.md Section 1, Step 2) are cross-set shared names (`Electrolyte diffusivity [m2.s-1]`, etc.), so `--params` works directly with any parameter set. 26	- `--protocol` legal values: 27	  - `1C_discharge` (1C discharge, 3600 s, 298.15 K) 28	  - `4C_charge_45C` (4C charge, 900 s, 318.15 K) 29	  - `5C_discharge` (5C high-rate discharge, 720 s — rate scenarios; **high rate recommends `--mode dfn`** — SPMe severely underestimates capacity at 5C) 30	  - `lowT_discharge` (1C discharge, -20 °C/253.15 K — low-temperature scenarios) 31	  - `overcharge` (first 1C discharge to lower cut-off, then 0.5C charge to upper cut-off +0.5 V — overcharge scenarios; output includes T_max_K) 32	  - `aging_1C_100cyc` (100 cycles of 1C constant-current charge/discharge, SEI ec reaction limited + isothermal; voltage limits taken from the parameter set itself) 33	  - `aging_1C_100cyc_45C` (same, but 45 °C/318.15 K high-temperature aging) 34	- `--cycles`: override aging cycle count (default 100) 35	- `--mode`: `spme` (default) / `dfn`; dfn solver failure auto-degrades to SPMe retry (output `model_used` records `"SPMe(fallback)"`) 36	- `--thermal`: `lumped` (default) / `isothermal`; non-isothermal output includes `T_max_K`. The aging protocol internally fixes isothermal; `--thermal`/`--plating` are ignored 37	- `--plating`: enable plating module (Chen2020 parameter set has no plating parameters; standard defaults injected at runtime), output includes `anode_potential_v` 38	- Input `--params`: `{"<PyBaMM parameter name>": value}` — parameter names validated against the chosen parameter set, typically written per the mapping table in SKILL.md Section 1, Step 2 39	- Output keys: `model_used`, `time_s`, `voltage_v`, `capacity_ah`, `T_max_K` (non-isothermal), `anode_potential_v` (--plating); aging protocol outputs `model_used`, `protocol: "aging"`, `cycle_numbers`, `capacity_ah_per_cycle`, `sei_thickness_nm_end` 40	- Errors: 41	  - `unknown protocol 'x'; legal: [...]` → fix protocol name 42	  - `unknown mode 'x'; legal: spme, dfn` → fix mode name 43	  - `unknown parameter name(s): ['...']` → parameter name not in the chosen parameter set; check key names/spelling per the SKILL.md Section 1, Step 2 mapping table 44	  - `base parameter set has no 'SEI kinetic rate constant [m.s-1]'; ...` → chosen system has no aging model (e.g., ORegan2022); aging protocol only on aging-capable sets (Chen2020/OKane2022 etc.); honestly record N/A for systems without aging models 45	  - SPMe solve failure (pybamm.SolverError traceback) → parameter combination invalid; adjust per SKILL.md Section 1, Step 5 fallback 46	- Aging-protocol note: under standard SEI models the capacity trajectory may show a non-monotonic climb-then-saturate artifact (lithium loss shifts the voltage window) — annotate honestly in reports/evaluation, do not treat as normal degradation; coating/doping vs baseline must compare on the same system 47	 48	## run-mlp — ML potential structure relaxation 49	 50	``` 51	bda run-mlp --in IN [--model MODEL] --out OUT 52	``` 53	 54	- `--model`: `mace` (default) / `chgnet` 55	- Input `--in`: `{"candidates": [{"smiles": "SMILES"}]}` 56	- Output: `{"candidates": [{"smiles": "SMILES", "metrics": {"energy_ev": f, "converged": bool}, "model": "mace"}]}` 57	- Errors: `invalid SMILES: '...'` → fix SMILES; `unknown model 'x'; legal: mace, chgnet` → fix model name; `failed to embed 3D structure for ...` → SMILES cannot be conformer-embedded, switch candidate 58	- Where used: Stage 2, once per model (mace and chgnet) 59	 60	## run-xtb — semi-empirical quantum single point 61	 62	``` 63	bda run-xtb --in IN --out OUT 64	``` 65	 66	- Input `--in`: `{"candidates": [{"smiles": "SMILES"}]}` 67	- Output: `{"candidates": [{"smiles": "SMILES", "metrics": {"homo_ev": f, "lumo_ev": f}}]}` 68	- Errors: 69	  - `xtb binary not found; install from https://github.com/grimme-lab/xtb/releases and put xtb.exe on PATH` → install xtb and add to PATH 70	  - `failed to embed 3D structure for ...` → switch candidate 71	  - `xtb failed: <last 500 chars of stderr>` → troubleshoot per stderr content (structure/convergence issues) 72	  - `failed to parse HOMO/LUMO from xtb output` / `failed to parse total energy from xtb output` → computation ran but output artifact missing; switch conformer or candidate and rerun 73	 74	## run-orca — true DFT endorsement (only closing Top-3) 75	 76	``` 77	bda run-orca --in IN --out OUT 78	``` 79	 80	- Input `--in`: `{"candidates": [{"smiles": "SMILES"}]}` 81	- Output: `{"candidates": [{"smiles": "SMILES", "endorsement": {"E_hartree": f, "homo_ev": f, "lumo_ev": f, "ie_ev": f, "ea_ev": f}}]}` — ie_ev/ea_ev are vertical ionization energy/electron affinity (voltage-window proxies) 82	- Per candidate: gas-phase geometry optimization of neutral/cation/anion three times (r2SCAN-3c + OPT, automatic single point after optimization); spin multiplicity derived from electron count parity per charge state (even→singlet, odd→doublet); max 3 retries per molecule; CPU-slow (~2–3 hours per molecule), only at closing; forbidden inside the funnel 83	- Errors: 84	  - `ORCA binary not