cs / stage results / true DFT-MD endorsement / final recommendation / design notes — seven sections), written to `<case_dir>/<out>` (default `report.html`) 111	- No log.jsonl → renders an empty report; no corresponding entry → section shows "no data yet" 112	- Errors: no custom validation; log-line JSON parse failure → traceback pointing at the line number 113	- Where used: last closing step; report content deterministically generated from log.jsonl, no extra LLM calls 114	 115	## run-comp — electrode composition screening (CHGNet periodic relaxation) 116	 117	``` 118	bda run-comp --in IN --out OUT 119	``` 120	 121	- **Environment requirement**: CUDA torch (GPU relaxation ~20 s/state); CPU torch relaxation does not converge (measured). Local `.venv` is CPU torch — use `D:/anaconda/envs/py312/python.exe -m bda run-comp ...` (py312 has chgnet/pymatgen/ase + torch 2.13.0+cu126) 122	- Input `--in`: `{"candidates": [{"formula": "Li(Ni0.7Mn0.05Co0.05Si0.1Mg0.1)O2", "name": "NMC-SiMg"}]}` — NMC811 lattice site substitution; TM fractions must sum to 1 123	- Output: `{"baseline": {NMC811 energy + Li metal reference}, "candidates": [{formula, realized_tm_counts, avg_voltage_v, capacity_mah_g, e_full_ev, e_delith_ev, converged, rel_stability_ev_atom}], "calibration_note"}` 124	- Definitions (stated honestly, written to the report): 125	  - Average voltage = −[E(Li_x2)−E(Li_x1)−n_removed·E_Li]/n_removed (x∈[0.3,1], includes Li metal reference; NMC811 self-calibration ≈3.82 vs literature 3.8 V) 126	  - Capacity = 0.7 Li × F/3.6 ÷ molar mass (theoretical proxy; NMC811 ≈194 mAh/g) 127	  - `rel_stability_ev_atom` is for within-batch relative ranking only (relaxation not strictly converged; energy difference for the same composition between two relaxations can be ~1 eV/atom) 128	  - `converged=false` is common (300-step FIRE with fmax 0.1 not reached) — energy at screening precision; annotate honestly 129	  - True endorsement: `run-qe` at closing (periodic DFT, next section) — insid