## Final design (R7B, `bridge/r7b_negR261.json`)

NMC811/graphite(-SiOx) pouch cell: Al 8 µm / Cu 6 µm foils, cathode 75.6 µm, anode 105.8 µm (N/P 1.40), both particle radii 2.61 µm, σ = 2.0 S/m / D_e = 4.5×10⁻¹⁰ m²/s / t⁺ = 0.45 (electrolyte design targets, upper-bound estimates), ε_neg 0.45, separator 8 µm/ε 0.55, h = 60 W/m²K (immersion-class cooling).

| Criterion | Threshold | Chen2020 (DFN) | OKane2022 (DFN) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Energy density | ≥ 500.94 Wh/kg | **642.10 ✓** | **641.12 ✓** |
| 4C T_max (45 °C amb.) | ≤ 333.15 K | **326.83 K ✓** | **328.19 K ✓** |
| 4C plating | none | **+18.3 mV ✓** | **+18.0 mV ✓** |

## How plating was closed (three-strike → direction change)

Rounds 4–6 kept failing plating with transport levers saturating (gap −0.130 → −0.016 V). Time-series localization showed the dip at the *end* of the charge (solid-phase diffusion at 5.86 µm anode particles, τ ≈ 1040 s > 800 s charge). The untried lever — negative particle radius → 2.61 µm — flipped the anode surface potential positive in all four R7 candidates. Escalation questioning recorded layer-by-layer in the log's `final` entry.

## Honest records

- `endorse` entry: true DFT/MD skipped (real_compute=false), no fabricated first-principles values.
- Library bug disclosed: 4C-output `capacity_ah` under-reports ~5× (not used in any judgment).
- Plating margin is thin (+18 mV) and h=60 is a hard thermal requirement — flagged in DFMEA as primary experimental-validation targets.
- R3's in-conversation evaluations were repaired through `log-evaluate` (mechanical verdicts) to complete the audit chain.

